// Dagric OS — keep the friendly app names true after every package operation.
//
// The renamed launcher entries live in /usr/local/share/applications, which
// wins over /usr/share/applications by XDG precedence and which dpkg never
// touches — so the rename itself already survives upgrades. What does NOT
// survive on its own is the REST of each copied file: shadowing a .desktop
// whole-file also freezes its Exec=, MimeType= and Desktop Actions at the
// moment it was written, so a future dolphin/okular upgrade that adds a MIME
// type or changes a command line would be masked by our stale copy.
//
// Re-deriving the overrides after each dpkg run fixes that: only the naming
// keys stay ours, everything else tracks whatever upstream now ships.
//
// Post-Invoke-Success (not Post-Invoke) so it runs only after dpkg actually
// succeeded, and the whole command is swallowed with `|| true`. An apt hook
// that can fail is an apt that can scare a non-technical owner with a red
// error over a cosmetic rename — this must never be the reason an update
// looks broken.
DPkg::Post-Invoke-Success {
    "if [ -x /usr/bin/dagric-app-names ]; then /usr/bin/dagric-app-names >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; fi";
};
